\n","```\n","\n","separately, you create:\n","\n","```text\n","scut_head/\n","├── train/\n","├── valid/\n","└── test/\n","```\n","\n","with both parts merged into each split.\n","\n","### Why you rename the files\n","\n","This is a very important part of your code.\n","\n","Suppose Part A and Part B both contain:\n","\n","```text\n","001.jpg\n","001.jpg\n","```\n","\n","If you copied both into the same directory without renaming them, one could overwrite the other.\n","\n","You therefore create:\n","\n","```python\n","new_name = f\"part{part_name}_{f.name}\"\n","```\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","Part A:\n","001.jpg\n","```\n","\n","becomes:\n","\n","```text\n","partA_001.jpg\n","```\n","\n","and:\n","\n","```text\n","Part B:\n","001.jpg\n","```\n","\n","becomes:\n","\n","```text\n","partB_001.jpg\n","```\n","\n","This prevents filename collisions.\n","\n","## Building the copy list\n","\n","You iterate through:\n","\n","```python\n","for part_name, part in [(\"A\", PART_A), (\"B\", PART_B)]:\n","```\n","\n","then:\n","\n","```python\n","for split in [\"train\", \"valid\", \"test\"]:\n","```\n","\n","then:\n","\n","```python\n","for folder in [\"images\", \"labels\"]:\n","```\n","\n","This effectively visits:\n","\n","```text\n","PartA/train/images\n","PartA/train/labels\n","PartA/valid/images\n","PartA/valid/labels\n","PartA/test/images\n","PartA/test/labels\n","\n","PartB/train/images\n","PartB/train/labels\n","PartB/valid/images\n","PartB/valid/labels\n","PartB/test/images\n","PartB/test/labels\n","```\n","\n","Each file is added to:\n","\n","```python\n","files_to_copy\n","```\n","\n","as a source/destination pair:\n","\n","```python\n","(src, dst)\n","```\n","\n","## Copying the dataset\n","\n","You use:\n","\n","```python\n","from tqdm.auto import tqdm\n","```\n","\n","to provide a progress bar.\n","\n","Then:\n","\n","```python\n","shutil.copy2(src, dst)\n","```\n","\n","copies each file.\n","\n","`copy2()` is useful because it attempts to preserve file metadata in addition to copying the file contents.\n","\n","The resulting structure is:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/scut_head/\n","\n","├── train/\n","│   ├── images/\n","│   │   ├── partA_...\n","│   │   ├── partA_...\n","│   │   ├── partB_...\n","│   │   └── ...\n","│   │\n","│   └── labels/\n","│       ├── partA_...\n","│       ├── partB_...\n","│       └── ...\n","│\n","├── valid/\n","│   ├── images/\n","│   └── labels/\n","│\n","└── test/\n","    ├── images/\n","    └── labels/\n","```"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"cfb83b0b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.552897Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.552123Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.558401Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.557742Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.015038,"end_time":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.559749+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.544711+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["/kaggle/working/scut_head.yaml\n"]}],"source":["import yaml\n","\n","dataset_yaml = {\n","    \"path\": str(COMBINED_PATH),\n","    \"train\": \"train/images\",\n","    \"val\": \"valid/images\",\n","    \"test\": \"test/images\",\n","    \"nc\": 1,\n","    \"names\": [\"head\"]\n","}\n","\n","yaml_path = Path(\"/kaggle/working/scut_head.yaml\")\n","\n","with open(yaml_path, \"w\") as f:\n","    yaml.dump(dataset_yaml, f, sort_keys=False)\n","\n","print(yaml_path)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ab54ad67","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006531,"end_time":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.573065+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.566534+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# YOLO\n","\n","![YOLO Architecture](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/spl_03/main/images/sparse/scut_head_yolo/architecture.png)\n","\n","## Creating the YOLO dataset YAML\n","\n","You then create:\n","\n","```python\n","dataset_yaml = {\n","    \"path\": str(COMBINED_PATH),\n","    \"train\": \"train/images\",\n","    \"val\": \"valid/images\",\n","    \"test\": \"test/images\",\n","    \"nc\": 1,\n","    \"names\": [\"head\"]\n","}\n","```\n","\n","This is the configuration that tells Ultralytics how to interpret your dataset.\n","\n","This file becomes the interface between your dataset and YOLO.\n","\n","### `path`\n","\n","```python\n","\"path\": str(COMBINED_PATH)\n","```\n","\n","The root dataset directory:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/scut_head\n","```\n","\n","### `train`\n","\n","```python\n","\"train\": \"train/images\"\n","```\n","\n","Training images are located at:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/scut_head/train/images\n","```\n","\n","### `val`\n","\n","```python\n","\"val\": \"valid/images\"\n","```\n","\n","Validation images are located at:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/scut_head/valid/images\n","```\n","\n","### `test`\n","\n","```python\n","\"test\": \"test/images\"\n","```\n","\n","Test images are located at:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/scut_head/test/images\n","```\n","\n","### `nc`\n","\n","```python\n","\"nc\": 1\n","```\n","\n","means there is exactly one object class.\n","\n","### `names`\n","\n","```python\n","\"names\": [\"head\"]\n","```\n","\n","means:\n","\n","```text\n","Class 0 = head\n","```\n","\n","Therefore a YOLO label line beginning with:\n","\n","```text\n","0\n","```\n","\n","represents a head."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"id":"bfcdfe92","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.588115Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.587589Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-26T08:44:33.050704Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-26T08:44:33.049695Z"},"papermill":{"duration":7767.472679,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:33.052682+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T06:35:05.580003+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\u001b[KDownloading htt