 Python-3.12.13 torch-2.10.0+cu128 CUDA:0 (Tesla T4, 14912MiB)\n","Model summary (fused): 92 layers, 25,840,339 parameters, 0 gradients, 78.7 GFLOPs\n","\u001b[K                 Class     Images  Instances      Box(P          R      mAP50  mAP50-95): 100% ━━━━━━━━━━━━ 55/55 1.8it/s 30.7s\n","                   all        866      22742       0.93      0.928      0.959      0.498\n","Speed: 0.8ms preprocess, 28.4ms inference, 0.0ms loss, 2.6ms postprocess per image\n","Results saved to \u001b[1m/kaggle/working/custom_yolo/head_detection\u001b[0m\n"]}],"source":["from ultralytics import YOLO\n","\n","# Load YOLOv8 medium model for better small object detection\n","yolo_custom = YOLO('yolov8m.pt', task='detect')\n","\n","# Configuration - HEAVILY OPTIMIZED FOR MAXIMUM DETECTION\n","CONFIG = {\n","    \"batch_size\": 8,  # Reduced for larger image size\n","    \"epochs\": 50,  # More epochs for better custom model training\n","    \"img_size\": 1280,  # Large size for detecting distant persons\n","    \"confidence_threshold\": 0.25,  # VERY LOW - detects even faint persons in rear rows\n","    \"iou_threshold\": 0.4,  # Slightly lower for better NMS\n","    \"max_det\": 500,  # Very high for crowded classrooms\n","    \"seed\": 42,\n","    \"patience\": 10\n","}\n","\n","\n","# Train on dataset\n","print(\"Starting training...\")\n","\n","results = yolo_custom.train(\n","        data=str(yaml_path),\n","        epochs=CONFIG['epochs'],\n","        imgsz=CONFIG['img_size'],\n","        batch=CONFIG['batch_size'],\n","        device=DEVICE,\n","        patience=CONFIG['patience'],\n","        save=True,\n","        verbose=True,\n","        project=\"/kaggle/working/custom_yolo\",\n","        name=\"head_detection\",\n","        exist_ok=False,\n","        seed=CONFIG['seed'],\n","        deterministic=True,\n","        # amp=False,\n","        # workers=0\n",")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3380a2c1","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.497734,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:33.960473+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:33.462739+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Loading YOLOv8m\n","\n","You then import:\n","\n","```python\n","from ultralytics import YOLO\n","```\n","\n","and load:\n","\n","```python\n","yolo_custom = YOLO('yolov8m.pt', task='detect')\n","```\n","\n","The model is:\n","\n","**YOLOv8 Medium — YOLOv8m**\n","\n","You are using a pretrained model rather than training the detector from scratch.\n","\n","Conceptually:\n","\n","```text\n","COCO-pretrained YOLOv8m\n","          │\n","          ▼\n","SCUT-HEAD fine-tuning\n","          │\n","          ▼\n","Head detector\n","```\n","\n","The model starts with general visual features learned from a large object-detection dataset and adapts them to your head-detection task.\n","\n","### Why YOLOv8m?\n","\n","For crowd scenes, heads can be relatively small, particularly for people far from the camera.\n","\n","Compared with a smaller model such as YOLOv8n, YOLOv8m has substantially more capacity.\n","\n","The trade-off is:\n","\n","```text\n","YOLOv8n\n","  ↓\n","faster / lighter\n","  ↓\n","less computational cost\n","\n","YOLOv8m\n","  ↓\n","larger / more computationally expensive\n","  ↓\n","greater model capacity\n","```\n","\n","## Training configuration\n","\n","You define:\n","\n","```python\n","CONFIG = {\n","    \"batch_size\": 8,\n","    \"epochs\": 50,\n","    \"img_size\": 1280,\n","    \"confidence_threshold\": 0.25,\n","    \"iou_threshold\": 0.4,\n","    \"max_det\": 500,\n","    \"seed\": 42\n","}\n","```\n","\n","Let's break these down.\n","\n","### Batch size\n","\n","```python\n","\"batch_size\": 8\n","```\n","\n","Eight images are processed together during each training iteration.\n","\n","A larger image size consumes considerable GPU memory, so batch size 8 is a reasonable memory-conscious choice.\n","\n","### Number of epochs\n","\n","```python\n","\"epochs\": 50\n","```\n","\n","The training dataset is potentially seen up to 50 times.\n","\n","One epoch means approximately:\n","\n","```text\n","entire training dataset → model\n","```\n","\n","50 epochs gives the model many opportunities to learn the SCUT-HEAD-specific features.\n","\n","### Image size\n","\n","```python\n","\"img_size\": 1280\n","```\n","\n","You train at:\n","\n","```text\n","1280 × 1280\n","```\n","\n","rather than a smaller resolution such as:\n","\n","```text\n","640 × 640\n","```\n","\n","This is particularly relevant to your application.\n","\n","In crowd scenes, distant heads may occupy only a small number of pixels. Increasing the input resolution can preserve more spatial information about small objects.\n","\n","The trade-off is significantly higher:\n","\n","* GPU memory usage\n","* training time\n","* inference cost\n","\n","### Confidence threshold\n","\n","You define:\n","\n","```python\n","\"confidence_threshold\": 0.25\n","```\n","\n","This is a relatively low detection threshold.\n","\n","During inference/evaluation, predictions with confidence below the selected threshold are discarded.\n","\n","Conceptually:\n","\n","```text\n","Prediction confidence\n","       │\n","       ├── 0.05 → reject\n","       ├── 0.10 → reject\n","       ├── 0.14 → reject\n","       └── 0.25+ → keep\n","```\n","\n","A lower threshold can increase recall because more candidate heads are retained.\n","\n","However, it can also increase false positives.\n","\n","An important point: this threshold is used during your later `model.val()` call because you explicitly pass:\n","\n","```python\n","conf=0.25\n","```\n","\n","It is **not a training hyperparameter** in the same sense as the learning rate.\n","\n","### IoU threshold\n","\n","You use:\n","\n","```python\n","\"iou_threshold\": 0.4\n","```\n","\n","IoU means:\n","\n","**Intersection over Union**\n","\n","It measures overlap between two bounding boxes:\n","\n","$$\n","IoU =\n","\\frac{\\text{Area of Intersection}}\n","{\\text{Area of Union}}\n","$$\n","\n","IoU is used by non-maximum suppression and evaluation-related procedures.\n","\n","Your relatively lower threshold affects how overlapping detections are handled.\n","\n","### Maximum detections\n","\n","You use:\n","\n","```python\n","\"max_det\": 500\n","```\n","\n","This allows up to 500 detections for an image during validation.\n","\n","This matters for crowd counting because an image can contain a large number of heads.\n","\n","A low maximum detection limit could artificially cap the possible count.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","Actual heads = 350\n","max_det = 100\n","```\n","\n","would make it impossible for the detector to output more than 100 detections under that configuration.\n","\n","With:\n","\n","```text\n","max_det = 500\n","```\n","\n","the cap is much less restrictive for the scenes you're targeting.\n","\n","### Random seed\n","\n","```python\n","\"seed\": 42\n","```\n","\n","A fixed seed improves reproducibility by controlling some random operations.\n","\n","You also use:\n","\n","```python\n","deterministic=True\n","```\n","\n","which further emphasizes reproducible behavior.\n","\n","It is important to note that complete reproducibility can still depend on the hardware, CUDA/PyTorch versions, and other environmental factors.\n","\n","## Training the detector\n","\n","The actual training starts here:\n","\n","```python\n","results = yolo_custom.train(\n","    data=str(yaml_path),\n","    epochs=CONFIG['epochs'],\n","    imgsz=CONFIG['img_size'],\n","    batch=CONFIG['batch_size'],\n","    device=DEVICE,\n","    patience=10,\n","    save=True,\n","    verbose=True,\n","    project=\"/kaggle/working/custom_yolo\",\n","    name=\"head_detection\",\n","    exist_ok=False,\n","    seed=CONFIG['seed'],\n","    deterministic=True,\n","    amp=False,\n","    workers=0\n",")\n","```\n","### Dataset argument\n","\n","```python\n","data=str(yaml_path)\n","```\n","\n","tells YOLO to use:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/scut_head.yaml\n","```\n","\n","The YAML tells YOLO where the training, validation, and testing images are located.\n","\n","### Early stopping\n","\n","You use:\n","\n","```python\n","patience=10\n","```\n","\n","This enables early stopping.\n","\n","If the monitored validation performance does not improve for 10 epochs, training can stop before reaching all 50 epochs.\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","maximum = 50 epochs\n","```\n","\n","but the actual training could finish earlier.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","Epoch 1\n","Epoch 2\n","...\n","Epoch 34\n","...\n","No improvement\n","...\n","Epoch 44\n","→ stop\n","```\n","\n","This helps reduce unnecessary training once validation performance has stopped improving.\n","\n","### Saving the model\n","\n","```python\n","save=True\n","```\n","\n","allows training artifacts and model checkpoints to be saved.\n","\n","Your training output is directed to:\n","\n","```python\n","project=\"/kaggle/working/custom_yolo\"\n","name=\"head_detection\"\n","```\n","\n","Therefore the main directory is:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/custom_yolo/head_detection/\n","```\n","\n","and the trained weights are expected under:\n","\n","```text\n","/kaggle/working/custom_yolo/head_detection/weights/\n","```\n","\n","including:\n","\n","```text\n","best.pt\n","last.pt\n","```\n","\n","Typically:\n","\n","* `best.pt` = checkpoint corresponding to the best validation performance\n","* `last.pt` = checkpoint from the final training epoch\n","\n","### AMP disabled\n","\n","You use:\n","\n","```python\n","amp=False\n","```\n","\n","AMP means **Automatic Mixed Precision**.\n","\n","With AMP enabled, suitable operations can use lower-precision arithmetic to reduce memory usage and potentially accelerate training.\n","\n","You explicitly disable it.\n","\n","This can be useful if you want more conservative numerical behavior or if mixed precision causes issues, but it may increase memory consumption and training time.\n","\n","### Workers = 0\n","\n","```python\n","workers=0\n","```\n","\n","means data loading uses no additional worker processes.\n","\n","This is sometimes useful in notebook environments, especially when multiprocessing creates instability.\n","\n","The downside is potentially slower data loading.\n","\n","### Training output\n","\n","The training process generates files such as:\n","\n","```text\n","custom_yolo/\n","└── head_detection/\n","    ├── weights/\n","    │   ├── best.pt\n","    │   └── last.pt\n","    ├── results.csv\n","    ├── results.png\n","    ├── confusion_matrix.png\n","    ├── confusion_matrix_normalized.png\n","    ├── BoxPR_curve.png\n","    ├── BoxF1_curve.png\n","    ├── BoxP_curve.png\n","    └── BoxR_curve.png\n","```\n","\n","The exact contents can vary with the Ultralytics version.\n","\n","## Loading the best trained model\n","\n","After training, you load:\n","\n","```python\n","model = YOLO(\n","    \"/kaggle/working/custom_yolo/head_detection/weights/best.pt\"\n",")\n","```\n","\n","This is the model you intend to use for evaluation and eventually for inference.\n","\n","The important point is that you are using:\n","\n","```text\n","best.pt\n","```\n","\n","rather than simply using the final checkpoint."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"7e6cb32c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T08:44:34.786737Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-26T08:44:34.786198Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-26T08:44:39.943296Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-26T08:44:39.94257Z"},"papermill":{"duration":5.574457,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:39.945707+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:34.37125+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","RESULTS_PATH = Path(\"/kaggle/working/custom_yolo/head_detection\")\n","\n","images = {\n","    \"results.png\": \"YOLO Model Training Results\",\n","    \"confusion_matrix.png\": \"Confusion Matrix\",\n","    \"confusion_matrix_normalized.png\": \"Normalized Confusion Matrix\",\n","    \"BoxPR_curve.png\": \"Precision–Recall Curve\",\n","    \"BoxF1_curve.png\": \"F1-Score Curve\",\n","    \"BoxP_curve.png\": \"Precision Curve\",\n","    \"BoxR_curve.png\": \"Recall Curve\",\n","}\n","\n","for image, title in images.items():\n","\n","    path = RESULTS_PATH / image\n","\n","    if path.exists():\n","\n","        img = plt.imread(path)\n","\n","        plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n","        plt.imshow(img)\n","        plt.title(title, fontsize=16, fontweight=\"bold\")\n","        plt.axis(\"off\")\n","        plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8cd467f0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.51284,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:40.887269+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:40.374429+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Training-result visualization\n","\n","You define:\n","\n","```python\n","RESULTS_PATH = Path(\n","    \"/kaggle/working/custom_yolo/head_detection\"\n",")\n","```\n","\n","Then:\n","\n","```python\n","images = {\n","    \"results.png\": \"YOLO Model Training Results\",\n","    \"confusion_matrix.png\": \"Confusion Matrix\",\n","    \"confusion_matrix_normalized.png\": \"Normalized Confusion Matrix\",\n","    \"BoxPR_curve.png\": \"Precision–Recall Curve\",\n","    \"BoxF1_curve.png\": \"F1-Score Curve\",\n","    \"BoxP_curve.png\": \"Precision Curve\",\n","    \"BoxR_curve.png\": \"Recall Curve\",\n","}\n","```\n","\n","You then check whether each file exists.\n","\n","If it exists, you load it using:\n","\n","```python\n","img = plt.imread(path)\n","```\n","\n","and display it.\n","\n","### `results.png`\n","\n","This is the main training-progress visualization.\n","\n","It generally contains curves related to:\n","\n","* training losses\n","* validation losses\n","* precision\n","* recall\n","* mAP\n","\n","The purpose is to understand how the model behaves across epochs.\n","\n","For example, you want to observe whether:\n","\n","```text\n","training loss ↓\n","validation loss ↓\n","precision ↑\n","recall ↑\n","mAP ↑\n","```\n","\n","over training.\n","\n","### Confusion matrix\n","\n","The confusion matrix provides information about classification/detection outcomes.\n","\n","Since you have only one class:\n","\n","```text\n","head\n","```\n","\n","the matrix is much simpler than a multi-class detection problem.\n","\n","It can help reveal:\n","\n","* correctly detected heads\n","* missed heads\n","* false detections\n","\n","For object detection, however, the interpretation differs somewhat from a simple classification confusion matrix because matching predictions to ground-truth boxes involves IoU.\n","\n","### Normalized confusion matrix\n","\n","```text\n","confusion_matrix_normalized.png\n","```\n","\n","normalizes the corresponding values, making relative proportions easier to interpret when counts differ significantly.\n","\n","### Precision–Recall curve\n","\n","```text\n","BoxPR_curve.png\n","```\n","\n","shows the relationship between:\n","\n","**Precision**\n","\n","and\n","\n","**Recall**\n","\n","as the confidence threshold changes.\n","\n","Precision:\n","\n","$$\n","Precision =\n","\\frac{TP}{TP+FP}\n","$$\n","\n","Recall:\n","\n","$$\n","Recall =\n","\\frac{TP}{TP+FN}\n","$$\n","\n","where:\n","\n","* TP = true positives\n","* FP = false positives\n","* FN = false negatives\n","\n","For head detection:\n","\n","#### High precision\n","\n","Means relatively few predicted heads are false positives.\n","\n","#### High recall\n","\n","Means the detector finds a large proportion of the actual heads.\n","\n","For crowd counting, recall is particularly relevant because missed heads directly contribute to under-counting.\n","\n","### F1 curve\n","\n","```text\n","BoxF1_curve.png\n","```\n","\n","shows F1 score across confidence thresholds.\n","\n","F1 is:\n","\n","$$\n","F1 =\n","2\\frac{Precision \\times Recall}\n","{Precision + Recall}\n","$$\n","\n","It balances precision and recall.\n","\n","### Precision curve\n","\n","```text\n","BoxP_curve.png\n","```\n","\n","shows precision as the confidence threshold changes.\n","\n","### Recall curve\n","\n","```text\n","BoxR_curve.png\n","```\n","\n","shows recall as the confidence threshold changes.\n","\n","This can help you understand how sensitive your detector is to the selected confidence threshold."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"id":"32f757b2","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T08:44:41.722142Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-26T08:44:41.721163Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-26T08:45:44.96004Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-26T08:45:44.958863Z"},"papermill":{"duration":63.658852,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:45:44.961795+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:44:41.302943+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Ultralytics 8.4.163 🚀 Python-3.12.13 torch-2.10.0+cu128 CUDA:0 (Tesla T4, 14912MiB)\n","Model summary (fused): 92 layers, 25,840,339 parameters, 0 gradients, 78.7 GFLOPs\n","\u001b[34m\u001b[1mval: \u001b[0mFast image 