n","```\n","\n","### Evaluation image size\n","\n","You again use:\n","\n","```python\n","imgsz=1280\n","```\n","\n","This is consistent with your training resolution.\n","\n","This is useful because changing the inference resolution can affect detection performance, particularly for small heads.\n","\n","### Evaluation batch size\n","\n","```python\n","batch=8\n","```\n","\n","means the validation process evaluates images in batches of 8, assuming GPU memory allows it.\n","\n","### Evaluation confidence threshold\n","\n","```python\n","conf=0.25\n","```\n","\n","means predictions below 0.25 confidence are excluded from the evaluation at that operating point.\n","\n","This is important for your thesis because the reported precision/recall values correspond to the evaluation configuration you selected.\n","\n","### Evaluation IoU threshold\n","\n","```python\n","iou=0.4\n","```\n","\n","sets the IoU-related evaluation/NMS configuration used by the Ultralytics validation process.\n","\n","You should report this configuration alongside your metrics if you want the experiment to be reproducible.\n","\n","### Evaluation maximum detections\n","\n","```python\n","max_det=500\n","```\n","\n","again prevents the detector from being artificially limited to a small number of predictions in crowded images.\n","\n","### Extracting precision\n","\n","You print:\n","\n","```python\n","metrics.box.mp\n","```\n","\n","which represents the mean precision across classes.\n","\n","Since you have only:\n","\n","```text\n","head\n","```\n","\n","the result effectively corresponds to the head class.\n","\n","You display it as:\n","\n","```python\n","print(f\"Precision : {metrics.box.mp:.4f}\")\n","```\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```text\n","Precision : 0.xxxx\n","```\n","\n","### Extracting recall\n","\n","You use:\n","\n","```python\n","metrics.box.mr\n","```\n","\n","which represents mean recall across classes.\n","\n","Again, because this is a single-class detector:\n","\n","```text\n","mean recall ≈ head recall\n","```\n","\n","### mAP@50\n","\n","You calculate:\n","\n","```python\n","metrics.box.map50\n","```\n","\n","This is:\n","\n","**mean Average Precision at IoU = 0.50**\n","\n","Usually abbreviated:\n","\n","```text\n","mAP@50\n","```\n","\n","A detection is considered a match when the predicted bounding box sufficiently overlaps the ground-truth box according to the IoU criterion.\n","\n","### mAP@50:95\n","\n","You calculate:\n","\n","```python\n","metrics.box.map\n","```\n","\n","This corresponds to the COCO-style mAP averaged over multiple IoU thresholds:\n","\n","```text\n","0.50\n","0.55\n","0.60\n","...\n","0.95\n","```\n","\n","This is generally a much stricter metric than mAP@50.\n","\n","So:\n","\n","```text\n","mAP@50\n","```\n","\n","answers roughly:\n","\n","> How well does the detector perform when a 0.50 IoU criterion is used?\n","\n","while:\n","\n","```text\n","mAP@50:95\n","```\n","\n","asks:\n","\n","> How well does the detector perform across increasingly strict localization criteria?\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"id":"f03bbb21","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T08:45:46.619067Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-26T08:45:46.618587Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-26T08:45:46.777631Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-26T08:45:46.776923Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.577018,"end_time":"2026-09-26T08:45:46.779178+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-26T08:45:46.20216+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Dataset downloaded to: /kaggle/input/datasets/masum1834e/public-transport-crowd-counting\n"]}],"source":["import kagglehub\n","\n","dataset_path = kagglehub.dataset_download(\"masum1834e/public-transport-crowd-counting\")\n","print(\"Dataset downloaded to:\", dataset_path)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":15,"id":"34521575","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-26T08:45:47.696632Z","iop